{#
    The rail shows the section the reader is in, while the bar carries the site.

    Both are the same entry read at a different level, worked out in
    `Navigation\Menu` because a template cannot derive ancestry. The section is
    the one entry marked `here` or `current`, and `Navigation\Rail` is that
    slice of it. The element gets the entry and owns all of its markup. Its
    label is the heading, its pages are the list, and a page with pages of
    its own is a fold.

    Nothing where the section is a single page. An absent rail is not an empty
    one, and the bar's name for the section is the whole of what there is to
    say.
#}
{%- set section = rail() -%}
{%- if section -%}
<sds-nav-rail entry="{{ section|json_encode }}"></sds-nav-rail>
{%- endif -%}
